WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.660
Welcome to Objective evidence and triangulation. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Develop an evidence-based way to examine actual practices..

2
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:22.590
Consider this scenario. A manager claims reviews occur, but records and project interviews are inconsistent. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:33.810
Start with two steps: State an explicit evaluation question. Then Collect artifacts and observations. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:44.680
Continue with Cross-check interviews and records. Then Record supported findings and open questions. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:55.940
Stronger evidence looks like this: Evidence of actual implementation. Weaker evidence would be: An unverified claim. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:10.190
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
